# Fixtures are byte-exact artefacts, not text.
#
# Without this, Git translates line endings on a Windows checkout and every
# fixture changes underneath the tests. It surfaced as tests/integration/
# cross_sdk_test.c failing on Windows only: proof_params.txt arrived with CRLF,
# strtok on "\n" left a trailing CR on the account and machine ids, and a proof
# bound to those ids stopped verifying.
#
# The .lic and .mach files were passing, but only by luck -- this SDK's PEM
# reader strips embedded whitespace, so it happened to tolerate the damage. A
# signature covers exact bytes; nothing should depend on that tolerance.
tests/fixtures/** -text
tests/fuzz/corpus/** -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not run.
*.sh text eol=lf
